Add native VS Code workspace for rumpelpod

Add a workspace extension that switches pods from an Activity Bar view.
Attach agent and shell sessions in sidebar xterm terminals. Show pod
changes in native VS Code multi-diff editors. Run CLI commands under a
packaged node-pty binding. Pod creation, lifecycle output, and
interactive sessions share the CLI's established terminal behavior.

Expose typed daemon endpoints for list and review snapshots plus live
invalidation events. Have the extension consume them directly over the
Unix socket without JSON CLI modes or an event subprocess. Notify review
clients from a bounded host post-receive hook while preserving user
hooks and custom daemon sockets. Keep this as the only new
terminal-related rumpel core surface. Do not retain the abandoned
daemon PTY streaming routes or API.

Publish separate Linux x64, Linux arm64, and macOS arm64 VSIX assets.
Build them in existing platform jobs. Preserve the multi-binary rumpel
tarball and installer. Build Linux bindings in a pinned Bullseye image.
Reject bindings above the supported glibc baseline. Keep normal pipeline
extension checks local so they do not start nested Docker builds.

Provide a loopback-only live code-server workspace backed by a small
anyhow demo repository and lingering user services. Run demo pods as a
non-root user because Claude rejects its permission bypass under root.
Persist only allowlisted agent credentials for those services. Install
the daemon units through rumpel system-install at image build instead
of vendoring copies, and let CI boots mask the browser service. Use the
same complete devcontainer image in development and CI, and report
startup logs when its entrypoint fails. Pin the arm64 code-server
archive to its published digest. Keep the timing-sensitive Playwright
test available only through the explicit ignored-test flag. Keep a
bounded terminal cache per pod so scrollback survives pod switches
while parser and mouse state remain isolated. Keep SSH integration
fixtures independent of ambient agents.
